  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "DMS (Delivery Management System)",
    "description": "•\tBeginning in 2009 I have worked on a desktop and web-driven business application called Delivery Management System (DMS), which provides customer management and billing for home delivery businesses.  I helped extend the existing desktop application by designing and implementing a customer website interface, with a database which synchronizes with the desktop application.  I have also designed and built numerous customer-requested enhancements and tools, meeting the needs of the business clients, as well as their delivery customers.  I have been instrumental in recruiting new clients to DMS, as well as working to move the system from a custom designed consulting project to a product/service which can meet the needs of a greater client base.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Mar 2009 - Present"
   },
   {
    "title": "DRAMA",
    "description": "•\tI was hired to work on a project to design a build a electronic medical record system called DRAMA.  The system focuses on tracking and monitoring premature infants that participate in the Neonatal Follow-up Program of the Utah Department of Health.  Working in a team of two, I participated in all aspects of this 2-year project, beginning with stakeholder interviews, requirements gathering, analysis and system design, and database structure design, all the way through coding, testing, documentation and deployment.  Since the beta release in 2009 I have functioned as the project manager, leading all aspects of maintenance including enhancement design, estimates, and coding.  I am currently responsible for all maintenance contracts and invoicing as well as functioning as the user support contact.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Jan 2007 - Jan 2016"
   }
  ],
